hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2766","Narrated to us by Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala', who said: Narrated to us by Sufyan, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, who said: I was reciting to Aisha (RA) the verse: \Indeed"","" as-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah\"" (Surah Al-Baqarah"","" 2:158). I said to her"","" \""I do not see any sin upon one who does not perform Tawaf (Sa'i) between them.\"" She replied"""""
"2767","Narrated to us by Isa ibn Ibrahim, who said: Narrated to us by Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Aisha (RA) informed him: Before the Ansar embraced Islam, and before Ghassan did, they used to invoke (make talbiyah for) Manat. Consequently, they felt religious scruple (was hesitant) to perform Tawaf between As-Safa and Al-Marwah. This was their established custom in those days"
"2768","\nNarrated to us Bakr ibn Khālid, on the authority of ʿĀṣim, on the authority of Anas ibn Mālik (RA), who said:\nThe Ansār used to dislike performing the Tawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah until the verse was revealed:\n*\Indeed"","" aṣ-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah.\""*\n[Qur'an 2:158]\n\nSalm ibn Junādah (RA) added:\nSo they began to perform the Tawāf between them."""""
